<div>
  <section class="catalogue-intro">
    <h2>Small controls. Complete behaviours.</h2><p>
      Submit an empty name to exercise validation. Correct it and save. Errors retain your choices; the example never writes to a database.
    </p>
  </section>
  <div class="catalogue-grid">
    <section class="catalogue-panel">
      <h2>Actions</h2><div class="wb-actions catalogue-space">
        <.button phx-click="exercise" class="wb-button">Primary action</.button><.button
          phx-click={JS.focus(to: "#example_name")}
          class="wb-button secondary"
        >Focus name field</.button><.button disabled class="wb-button">Unavailable</.button>
      </div><p>
        Primary actions commit the current task. Secondary actions retain context. Unavailable actions remain identifiable.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section class="catalogue-panel">
      <h2>Named states</h2><div class="wb-actions catalogue-space">
        <Workbench.status label="Draft" /><Workbench.status label="Received" tone="success" /><Workbench.status
          label="Part received"
          tone="warning"
        /><Workbench.status label="Needs correction" tone="error" />
      </div><Workbench.notice id="control-notice" tone="warning">
        8 of 24 units received. The order stays open for the remaining 16.
      </Workbench.notice>
    </section>
    <section class="catalogue-panel">
      <h2>Fields & validation</h2><.form
        for={@form}
        id="example-form"
        phx-submit="control_submit"
        class="wb-form"
      >
        <.input
          field={@form[:name]}
          label="Customer name"
          class="wb-input"
          error_class="wb-input wb-invalid"
        />
        <.input
          field={@form[:status]}
          label="Status"
          type="select"
          options={~w(Draft Ready)}
          class="wb-input"
        />
        <.button class="wb-button" phx-disable-with="Saving…">Save example</.button>
      </.form><Workbench.notice :if={@result} id="control-result" tone="success">
        {@result}
      </Workbench.notice>
    </section>
    <section class="catalogue-panel">
      <h2>State conventions</h2><dl class="wb-facts">
        <div>
          <dt>Empty</dt><dd>Explain the next action</dd>
        </div><div>
          <dt>Invalid</dt><dd>Keep input; name the problem</dd>
        </div><div>
          <dt>Pending</dt><dd>Show progress</dd>
        </div><div>
          <dt>Success</dt><dd>Show the changed result</dd>
        </div><div>
          <dt>Conflict</dt><dd>Preserve and reconcile</dd>
        </div>
      </dl><p>
        Pending and cross-session conflict examples will need their own demonstrated stories before those patterns are marked verified.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</div>
